Pages = {94-99},
Note = {10th European Conference on Management Leadership and Governance
   (ECMLG), VERN Univ Appl Sci, Zagreb, CROATIA, NOV 13-14, 2014},
Abstract = {This article demonstrates the importance to anticipate and understand
   cultural differences and be able to adjust to workplace diversity in
   terms of cultural awareness and appropriate perception of such key
   factors as mission statement, corporate initiative, working rhythm and
   communication style. Mankind has entered the 21st century where the
   process of globalization influences many aspects of human life. To
   succeed one has to be able to do business in different cultural and
   linguistic environment. In reality the bigger a company becomes and the
   more national borders it crosses, the harder it has to work to conform
   to the central norm or party line that is so vital for its
   sustainability and prosperity. Firstly, the article illustrates the
   consequences of different cultural norms, customs and traditions,
   religion, beliefs and other factors of party lines that can cause
   misunderstanding, conflict and stress and steps that should be taken in
   order to succeed in running business internationally. Secondly, the
   paper contains a brief overview of cultural peculiarities in Kazakhstan.
   It is based on the survey conducted among MBA students of a joint
   programme with Maastricht School of Management in Kazakhstan. Thirdly,
   the findings of the study suggest that more profound research should be
   conducted among different social groups in the major companies of
   Kazakhstan.},
