   Kota Kinabalu, MALAYSIA, APR 19-21, 2016},
Abstract = {` Background: Public health education in Indonesia faces a
   multidimensional understanding and perception among providers, users,
   and stakeholders as well as its diversity. A university in Indonesia is
   obligated to make a center of excellent in the focus of interest
   according to the priority need of its society. Aim: The purpose of this
   evaluation research was to provide the best example of the effort and
   investment to advance research and education for Public Health in
   Coastal and Tropical Developments at Diponegoro University. Method: The
   method used in this qualitative research utilized secondary data,
   stakeholders' overview report review and participant observation.
   Results: Faculty of Public Health at Diponegoro University embraced the
   educational focus of interest, research agenda and community engagement
   to improve the health status of the people in the tropical and coastal
   region. The faculty conducted initial mapping on public health main
   problems in the coastal area. Subsequently, the collaboration work with
   the Ministry of Health in Indonesia, International Non-Government
   Organization as well as alumni and other sectors enhanced the effort and
   advancement of the educational and research in coastal and Tropical
   regions. Conclusion. Multi-sectoral inter-collaborations is the
   significant contributor to the success in advancing research and
   education in Public Health for Coastal and Tropical related
   developments.},
