Organization = {US DHHS, Agcy Tox Subst Dis Registry; NCI, Occupat Epidemiol Brach;
   NIEHS, Superfund Bas Res Program; Pan Amer Hlth Org; Univ Amer Puebla;
   World Meteorol Org},
Abstract = {Multiplication of irregular settlements surrounding outstanding
   economical development centers has originated deterioration of their
   inhabitants' environmental conditions. In this work we studied the
   influence of inadequate water supply in health and environmental
   standards of an irregular settlement, located in the state of Mexico. It
   lacks of most of public services (p. e. water distribution system,
   sewage, pavement). Water supply is available mainly by tank-trucks, and
   old industrial 200 liter-drums are used for domestic storage.
   An inquiry on sanitary conditions, health and inhabitant's perception on
   life quality (including problems derived from insufficient water supply)
   was done; physicochemical and bacteriological analyses of drinking water
   in 80 houses were done. Total and fecal coliforms were detected
   exceeding current local standards in more than 90\% of the samples.
   Average water consumption was estimated in 24 L/inhabitant/day. though
   22\% of the families use less than 24 10 L/inhabitant/day, though
   L/inhabitant/day.
   The quality of the supplied water was acceptable, but it suffers
   bacteriological deterioration due its careless management and
   settlement's unfavorable conditions, thus becoming an infection vehicle.
   The high incidence of gastrointestinal illnesses among infants has
   several routes: air, soil's direct contact, food and drinking water.
   Finally, different water supply alternatives and their economic and
   social feasibility are discussed.},
