   City, LITHUANIA, NOV 08-10, 2007},
Organization = {Lithuanian Univ Agr},
Abstract = {The agrifood products and gastronomy of the Castilla and Leon region in
   Spain are rich and is supported by the thousand of agrifood fairs
   celebrated around the region during the year. The work analyses the
   agrifood fairs celebrated in the region and their contribution to the
   rural development of the area, support the comercialization of agrifood
   products, maintain the traditions, promote the quality traditional
   products and promote the visit of tourists to the region. To analyse the
   agrifood fairs in Castilla and Leon were identified the Oficial Agrar
   Fairs in the region and to analyse the visitors perception primary
   sources like personal surveys were used. Frequencies and acumulated
   percent were obtained and by contingency tables the relationship between
   the interest in agrifood fairs of the visitors and other variables have
   been analysed. The work concludes that the reasons to visit the fairs
   are, pastime, turism, casuality or interest in traditional agrifood
   products. The tourists used to be the first time they visit the fair and
   the ones which repeat more the visit to the fairs are the interested in
   agrifood products. The tourists knew about the fair by recomendation or
   casuality, the local inhabitants by Tourist information office or
   Council and the interested in agrifood products by press.},
