Abstract = {This paper takes Yellow River Golden Triangle area as object of study,
   with method of grid cost weighted distance and GIS spatial analysis
   tool, it analyzes traffic accessibility of regions and county-level
   administrative units. Result shows that overall accessibility in Yellow
   River Golden Triangle area is still relatively lower, traffic
   accessibility in county-level administrative units has higher
   difference, traffic accessibility administrative units is imbalance,
   space distribution in traffic facilities in the regions is imbalance.
   Yellow River Golden Triangle area needs to strengthen construction of
   high-speed rail, highways and other modern transportation facilities,
   optimize spatial layout of road network, provides efficient and
   convenient transportation facilities for provincial border regional
   cooperation and development.},
