   (EENVIRO), Bucharest, ROMANIA, OCT 16-21, 2022},
Organization = {Constructii Erbasu SA; Romstal; Dantec Dynam; MetrOptics; European Univ
   Smart Urban Coastal Sustainabil; Tech Univ Civil Engn Bucharest, Fac
   Civil, Ind \& Agr Construct; Sustainable Solut Energy \& Environm},
Abstract = {Sediment transport plays an important role in the overall process of
   navigation along the rivers, as it shapes the fairway continuously. This
   paper aims to present the partial results obtained in the PhD research
   regarding measures to be used in order to help stabilize the channel
   bed. The measures have been proposed and tested based on a calibrated
   and validated 2 dimensional hydrodynamic and sediment transport model.
   The results show the influence of the proposed measures along the river
   channel in comparison to the situation where no measures would be taken
   at all. Furthermore it can help understand the river and sediment
   dynamics in order to make the best decision upon the location,
   orientation, geometry and other properties of the proposed measures.},
