   Smart Urban Coastal Sustainabil; Tech Univ Civil Engn Bucharest, Fac
   Civil, Ind \& Agr Construct; Sustainable Solut Energy \& Environm},
Abstract = {This paper presents a series of physical tests used to model cylindrical
   shafts in order to study the earth pressure distribution and the induced
   vertical and horizontal displacements of the adjacent soil. Various
   methods used to model cylindrical shafts are described: one or more semi
   -circular aluminium tubes, curved steel segments cut longitudinally or a
   latex bag filled with a heavy fluid. The results showed that the lateral
   earth pressure distribution is well correlated with the results based on
   Terzaghi's and Berezantzev's theories. Also, the lateral earth pressure
   decreases until the active wall displacement is occurred. Based on the
   physical tests, researchers developed a series of equations that can be
   used to calculate the vertical and horizontal displacements of the soil.},
