Note = {INTERNATIONAL CONF ON THE PEOPLES ROLE IN WETLAND MANAGEMENT, LEIDEN,
   NETHERLANDS, JUN 05-08, 1989},
Abstract = {The coexistence of intensive dairy farming and important nature values
   in the peat polder district in The Netherlands is highly appreciated. 
   However, owing to the still increasing agricultural pressure, the
   equilibrium between farmer and nature is being disturbed at the expense
   of the latter.  Government as well as private organizations for nature
   conservation are looking for possibilities to preserve this equilibrium.
   In this contribution, both existing and possible new instruments are
   treated briefly.  The instruments are divided into those that need a
   permanent external financial incentive and those that can do without
   such stimuli.},
